ce it.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Frequently Asked Questions</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Q: How long is the game?</strong><br>A: There are 3 modes. The shortest mode can be cleared in around <strong>15 minutes</strong>.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Q: What is the goal of the game?</strong><br>A: To reach a target <strong>experiment room number</strong>.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Q: Are there difficulty settings?</strong><br>A: Yes! There are <strong>three levels</strong>: Easy, Normal, and Hard\u2014fun for beginners and veterans alike.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Q: What happens if I find bugs or issues?</strong><br>A: Please leave a review! We\u2019ll try to address them in future <strong>updates</strong>.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Q: How long is one session?</strong><br>A: Anywhere from <strong>10 to 60 minutes</strong>, depending on play style and mode.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Download now on Steam!</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Title</strong>: <i>10-Second Rule</i><br><strong>Genre</strong>: Action, Horror, 8-ban-like, Solo Indie Game<br><strong>Publisher</strong>: Nosan<br><strong>Demo Release Date</strong>: July 23<br><strong>Full Release Date</strong>: February 11<br><strong>Price at Launch</strong>: 390 yen</p>",
